# Crustum Tessera

Prefer package docs and the `tessera-development` skill for orientation.

@scoped(['config/tessera.php', 'config/bootstrap.php'])
## Tessera config
- Load `config/tessera.php` after manifest install; publish via plugin-manifest (no dedicated install command).
- Set access / refresh / personal-access TTLs independently (`Tessera::tokensExpireIn` etc.).
- Register scopes with `Tessera::tokensCan(...)`; enable Password/Implicit grants only when required.
- Wire auth once: `TokenAuthenticator` before Session when Bearer must win; League `ResourceServer` from the container — see skill.
@endscoped

@scoped(['src/Model/Entity/**', 'src/Model/Table/**'])
## OAuth user
- User entity must implement `OAuthenticatable` and use `HasApiTokensTrait`.
- Attach Tessera users Behavior / associations on the Users table when linking clients and tokens.
@endscoped

@scoped(['config/routes.php', 'src/Middleware/**'])
## Token middleware & SPA
- Enforce scopes with named route middleware: `CheckTokenMiddleware` (all scopes) or `CheckTokenForAnyScopeMiddleware` (any).
- Pass required scopes as middleware constructor args; use `EnsureClientIsResourceOwnerMiddleware` for client-credentials style.
- SPA cookie auth: `CreateFreshApiTokenMiddleware`; prefer documented CSRF/cookie setup over ad hoc `ignoreCsrfToken()`.
@endscoped

@scoped(['tests/**'])
## Tessera tests
- Prefer `Tessera::actingAs()` / `actingAsClient()` (+ `clearActingAs()`); `TesseraTestCase` when available.
@endscoped
